    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0142" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6711/94</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Turkish Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Rustem</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 20, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your Note of the 19th instant replying to my communication of the 8th [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">12th</hi>] concerning certain statements made by me in
                    an interview with a press representative.</p>
                <p>In answer I beg that you will inform the President that I regret not to be able
                    to accept his point of view in the matter and that, in consequence, it appeared
                    to me necessary to ask my Government to grant me leave of absence. My departure
                    for Constantinople will take place within a fortnight.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Rustem</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
